Bob the tourist sacrificed a few more times and was finally granted 
Mjollnir. He then took on the Castle and got orange dragon scales. 
Unfortunately, he was trying to go wishless (and genoless and 
polyselfless), and had already used up all the ?oEA he had. He tried 
polypiling for ?oEA, but no luck, so he stuck the scales in his BoH and 
jumped down the trap door. The priest of Moloch got what he deserved, and 
Bob got a nice robe. Hmmm. Spellcasting still blocked by wearing mithril. 
Oh well, he'd find a ?oEA somewhere.

Asmodeus, Juiblex, Orcus, Vlad; got a nice Candelabrum, but not the 
scroll I'm looking for. Tried polypiling again with the scrolls I'd found 
along the way; finally got 3 precious ?oEA, which I promptly blessed. 
Took out a potion of booze (saved for such a special occasion), put on 
the orange dragon scales, quaffed the potion, read the scroll, 
mispronounced the words...."Your orange dragon scales are covered with a 
golden sheen." Huh? Back to the spoilers. Oh, ?oEA *not* confused is what 
creates DSM. Duh. I've just fooproofed my naturally fooproof dragon 
scales. Sigh. So I apply my unihorn, read the second scroll, and use the 
third scroll on a helm of brilliance I found in Orcustown. Cool! Even 
with iron shoes I can still spellcast reasonably reliably. 

So my AC isn't quite as good as it would have been without blowing the 
first scroll, but it's decent, so I keep exploring downward 
(incidentally, using the Heck2 patch, which has more opportunity for open 
spaces/rooms to be created in the mazes--nice). You know, the combination 
of spellcasting as a non-wizard, wearing two rings and an amulet, and the 
travel command, all combine to make me hungry a lot more often than I 
expect. No problem, I occasionally eat corpses and I have food rations.

Except all of a sudden I haven't checked the status line, and I'm 
fainting. Look in my BoH. No food rations, but a tin of blue dragon meat 
I tinned earlier. Pull it out. "It is not so easy to open this tin," and 
I faint again. Look in the BoH again: nothing but tripe rations, eggs, 
sprigs of wolvesbane, and fortune cookies. Try eating some of these (with 
unihorn application where needed), but don't get enough nutrition to get 
out of "fainting" status. Okay, I'll polymorph some of what I do have; 
hopefully I'll get something more nutritious. Five tripe rations come 
together to form a flesh golem.

I keep fainting, and I'm starting to get really scared that I'm going to 
starve to death here in Gehennom. Okay, screw wishless conduct. I rub the 
blessed magic lamp I've been using as a light source. "You freed me!" and 
now I have a peaceful djinni fighting the flesh golem (I was wearing a 
ring of conflict, I think). No wish. Great. So I pull out the Castle 
Wand, and zap. Q - a horn of plenty. Apply the horn of plenty. W - a tin. 
Apply the horn of plenty again. X - a tripe ration. I'm gonna starve to 
death trying to apply a horn of plenty. Finally get a food ration, eat, 
and pull myself together.

Whew! Close one. Well, I've blown wishless conduct already; may as well 
wish for a magic marker and get my armor really enchanted up. Levelport 
up to my main stash in the main dungeon, where I have a bunch of blank 
scrolls. Wish for a magic marker, and start writing blessed scrolls of 
enchant armor. What do I want to enchant first? Let's make it the ODSM. A 
couple of scrolls later, "Your armor violently glows silver for a while, 
then evaporates." Oh yeah; can't safely enchant +4 armor. So now I've 
lost my DSM.

Time to save game. Come back when *well* rested.

